1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,080
This is the GS1 Digital Link app.

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:12,835
It takes your product data from GS1 and turns it
into product pages on the website.

3
00:00:12,835 --> 00:00:20,040
Then it registers every barcode with GS1, so
scanning the QR code on a pack opens the right page.

4
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,795
In this video, we'll walk through one batch in
'both' mode:

5
00:00:23,795 --> 00:00:27,450
the website pages first, then the GS1 links.

6
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:33,550
Everything here uses a demo client with made-up
products, so nothing real gets touched.

7
00:00:34,195 --> 00:00:37,350
On the left, you'll see the four steps of a batch:

8
00:00:37,350 --> 00:00:40,630
Data, Content, Preflight, and Publish.

9
00:00:40,630 --> 00:00:43,110
You go through them in that order.

10
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:46,865
Below them, Setup and Runs belong to this machine.

11
00:00:46,865 --> 00:00:49,270
And that red 'production' label?

12
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:54,770
It means this app writes to the live website, and to
the real GS1 register.

13
00:00:55,402 --> 00:00:57,407
Step one is Data.

14
00:00:57,407 --> 00:01:00,462
First, upload the product selection list.

15
00:01:00,462 --> 00:01:04,712
That's the Excel file with the barcodes you want in
this batch.

16
00:01:05,346 --> 00:01:08,301
Next, the export from My GS1.

17
00:01:08,301 --> 00:01:10,906
The app reads every product in it.

18
00:01:10,906 --> 00:01:13,006
Here, that's twelve.

19
00:01:13,639 --> 00:01:16,119
The third upload is optional.

20
00:01:16,119 --> 00:01:22,174
It's the video sign-off sheet, where the client
confirms which video belongs to which barcode.

21
00:01:22,174 --> 00:01:26,674
Before anything's saved, the app shows you exactly
what would change.

22
00:01:27,312 --> 00:01:30,792
Any row it can't use is listed, with the reason.

23
00:01:30,792 --> 00:01:36,892
Here, Excel has turned a barcode into scientific
notation, and the screen tells you how to fix that

24
00:01:36,892 --> 00:01:37,872
in the sheet.

25
00:01:37,872 --> 00:01:39,927
The rest still applies.

26
00:01:39,927 --> 00:01:43,402
Click apply, and the video mapping is updated.

27
00:01:44,057 --> 00:01:46,937
Now, choose what this batch publishes.

28
00:01:46,937 --> 00:01:51,217
'Pages' writes website pages only, and those can be
undone.

29
00:01:51,217 --> 00:01:55,972
'Links' registers GS1 links for pages that already
exist.

30
00:01:55,972 --> 00:01:58,902
'Both' does the pages first, then the links.

31
00:01:58,902 --> 00:02:00,657
We'll pick both.

32
00:02:00,657 --> 00:02:02,612
Notice the warning:

33
00:02:02,612 --> 00:02:06,187
a GS1 record can never be deleted.

34
00:02:06,838 --> 00:02:09,643
Coverage gives you the batch at a glance.

35
00:02:09,643 --> 00:02:12,123
How many products are selected.

36
00:02:12,123 --> 00:02:14,053
How many can run.

37
00:02:14,053 --> 00:02:16,608
Which barcodes aren't in the export.

38
00:02:16,608 --> 00:02:21,013
Which can't run, because data is missing or there
are two videos.

39
00:02:21,013 --> 00:02:24,388
And which will go live without a video, for now.

40
00:02:25,313 --> 00:02:30,343
Below that is every product on your list, with its
status and the reason.

41
00:02:30,343 --> 00:02:32,723
A tick means it's in this batch.

42
00:02:32,723 --> 00:02:35,473
Untick anything you'd like to leave out.

43
00:02:36,119 --> 00:02:40,349
The issue report lists every problem, product by
product.

44
00:02:40,349 --> 00:02:45,429
You can download it as a PDF or Excel file and send
it to the client.

45
00:02:45,429 --> 00:02:50,179
Product data is always fixed in My GS1, never in
this app.

46
00:02:50,813 --> 00:02:54,438
Next saves your selection, and opens step two.

47
00:02:55,070 --> 00:02:59,775
Content is about the two bits of text a machine
writes for each page:

48
00:02:59,775 --> 00:03:02,280
the tagline, and the feature list.

49
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:07,210
Everything else on the page comes straight from GS1,
and is never made up.

50
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:11,990
'Check the live site' asks the website which pages
are missing that text.

51
00:03:11,990 --> 00:03:17,695
If an Anthropic key is filled in on the Setup
screen, a Generate button writes it for you.

52
00:03:17,695 --> 00:03:21,795
In this demo, the text is already there, so let's
move on.

53
00:03:25,639 --> 00:03:29,569
Preflight checks everything before a single thing is
written.

54
00:03:29,569 --> 00:03:32,924
The settings, the batch, the text, and the videos.

55
00:03:32,924 --> 00:03:37,329
Then it logs in to WordPress, and asks GS1 for a
token.

56
00:03:37,329 --> 00:03:39,259
Green means fine.

57
00:03:39,259 --> 00:03:42,189
Amber is a warning that's worth a read.

58
00:03:42,189 --> 00:03:44,094
Red stops you:

59
00:03:44,094 --> 00:03:47,294
Next only opens once nothing has failed.

60
00:03:47,970 --> 00:03:52,425
This demo has no passwords, so the three login
checks are red.

61
00:03:52,425 --> 00:03:55,305
On your machine, they should all be green.

62
00:03:55,305 --> 00:03:58,405
For the demo, we'll skip straight to Publish.

63
00:04:01,568 --> 00:04:05,423
Publish works through a series of gates, one at a
time.

64
00:04:05,423 --> 00:04:09,748
Nothing's written until every required gate has an
answer.

65
00:04:10,386 --> 00:04:13,366
The first gate confirms what this batch does:

66
00:04:13,366 --> 00:04:15,371
pages, and links.

67
00:04:15,371 --> 00:04:17,121
Confirm.

68
00:04:17,756 --> 00:04:19,836
Next, the text check.

69
00:04:19,836 --> 00:04:21,816
Eighteen pages:

70
00:04:21,816 --> 00:04:24,396
one per product, per language.

71
00:04:24,396 --> 00:04:26,576
And they all have their text.

72
00:04:26,576 --> 00:04:30,206
If you haven't read it yet, do that on the Content
screen.

73
00:04:30,206 --> 00:04:32,481
Here, the copy is good.

74
00:04:33,116 --> 00:04:35,171
Now, build the plan.

75
00:04:35,171 --> 00:04:37,176
This is the run sheet.

76
00:04:37,176 --> 00:04:42,451
Which pages get created, which live pages would
change, and which are left alone.

77
00:04:43,089 --> 00:04:45,794
'All' runs every new and changed row.

78
00:04:45,794 --> 00:04:48,749
'New only' leaves live pages alone.

79
00:04:48,749 --> 00:04:54,829
'Review changed' lets you apply or skip each changed
page, or apply them all in one go.

80
00:04:54,829 --> 00:04:58,029
Every page here is new, so we'll choose all.

81
00:04:58,662 --> 00:05:03,442
Because this run writes to GS1, there's a separate
production check.

82
00:05:03,442 --> 00:05:05,897
Type the client name to confirm.

83
00:05:05,897 --> 00:05:07,527
Remember:

84
00:05:07,527 --> 00:05:09,827
these records are permanent.

85
00:05:10,463 --> 00:05:12,618
Then comes the dry run.

86
00:05:12,618 --> 00:05:16,173
It's exactly the same run, but nothing is written.

87
00:05:16,173 --> 00:05:22,228
It needs no passwords, and it lists what it would
do, for every product and every language.

88
00:05:22,228 --> 00:05:24,528
Read it before you go on.

89
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:31,275
If anything looks off here, like a barcode you
didn't expect, or a missing language, just cancel.

90
00:05:31,275 --> 00:05:33,575
Nothing's been written yet.

91
00:05:34,208 --> 00:05:36,788
And this is where the demo stops.

92
00:05:36,788 --> 00:05:40,418
On a real run, you'd press Proceed, and then, 'Write
it'.

93
00:05:40,418 --> 00:05:45,973
The app creates or updates the WordPress pages
first, with their images and videos.

94
00:05:45,973 --> 00:05:52,303
Then it registers each barcode with GS1, and saves
the QR codes in the output folder.

95
00:05:52,303 --> 00:05:55,458
Running a batch twice never makes duplicates.

96
00:05:55,458 --> 00:05:58,633
An existing page is simply updated.

97
00:05:59,277 --> 00:06:02,732
When the run's done, the summary lists every row.

98
00:06:02,732 --> 00:06:08,662
And a scan check confirms that each barcode opens
the right page, in Dutch and in French.

99
00:06:08,662 --> 00:06:12,012
The Runs screen keeps a report of every run.

100
00:06:12,646 --> 00:06:14,651
So that's one batch.

101
00:06:14,651 --> 00:06:17,931
Data, Content, Preflight, and Publish.

102
00:06:17,931 --> 00:06:19,661
And always:

103
00:06:19,661 --> 00:06:21,711
dry run first.
